  "title": "two processes writing one board lose no task",
  "requirement": "The board file has one writer at a time across processes: the read-modify-write holds a directory lock with a wait and a stale takeover, so two processes that create tasks into the same .dsh/taskboard.json both land every row, and no lock is left behind.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "stale",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "plugins/taskboard/test/board-lock.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test plugins/taskboard/test/board-lock.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "node --test plugins/taskboard/test/board-lock.test.mjs",
    "Red first: TASKBOARD_MODULE=.dsh/red-first/taskboard.mjs node --test plugins/taskboard/test/board-lock.test.mjs (module materialised from git HEAD)",
    "The test spawns two real node processes that each create 25 tasks through the plugin's createService against one board file, then reads the file"
  ],
  "expected": "All 50 titles are present with unique ids and no .lock directory remains; a stale lock is taken over and released; a writer waits for a young lock instead of writing through it. On the pre-fix module 25 of 50 tasks are lost (the later rename drops the earlier writer's rows).",
